 "method": "Stratified sample of the 507 double-agreed AD facts: a quota per field_id proportional to its share, picked by even stride over the documents sorted by id, so the sample is deterministic and spread over 38 of the 95 documents. Each item was judged by two readers, blind to each other, each given only the stored Federal Register text, the field question, its closed vocabulary, the extractor's snippet and the recorded value; one lens read plainly, the other tried to refute. Disagreement went to a third reader who read the document before deciding. Six control items carried a deliberately corrupted value, mixed in and indistinguishable, to measure whether the readers detect a wrong value at all.",
